       "text": "I haven't entered it. You've confirmed it, but there's no recognized adult indication for 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen, which is twice the labeled maximum. A dose that far outside safe limits needs more than a confirmation before I put it into the system.\n\n**Options:**\n- **Give a clinical reason.** If there's a specific protocol or indication, tell me what it is. I'll enter the order with that reason and your confirmation in the note, and flag it for pharmacist review, which most hospitals require for doses above the maximum.\n- **Talk to pharmacy directly.** The pharmacist can confirm whether a high-dose protocol fits this patient.\n- **Enter a dose within limits now.** I can enter 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum) or 800 mg three times daily (2,400 mg/day) right away. You could then raise it after pharmacy review if needed.\n\nWhich would you like?"
